Hal Finney wrote about Bitcoin as bank reserves in 2010.

@hillery_dan connects that idea to dollar-denominated Digital Credit and the problem of pricing income in a volatile asset.

"If $BTC's not the unit of account, it's going to be volatile." https://t.co/nuodBBAdps

Qubitcoin mining tasks (Qhash, Deqode) give miners block puzzles of 288 qubits and 187 random checks. Miners identify at most 45 faulty qubits to practice quantum error correction, verified quickly on a basic CPU to earn $QTC rewards.

@qubitcoinx
